complex-video-time.ts adapts the scoped fixed-rate CFR startup and encoder
deadline behavior of video_sync_process and adjust_frame_pts_to_encoder_tb in
FFmpeg fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c at commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.

This adaptation is licensed under GNU LGPL version 2.1 or, at your option, any
later version. The complete license is in LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.
The pinned upstream source is available in upstream/ffmpeg. The adaptation
handles a single fixed-rate finite rawvideo source and does not implement the
general FFmpeg synchronization engine. This notice does not assign a license
to the whole project or complete its project-wide license audit.

video-output/sync.ts and output-clock.ts adapt fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c encoder
synchronization and clock selection at the pinned commit above.
output-clock.ts also adapts libavfilter/vf_stack.c frame-rate comparison
(Copyright (c) 2015 Paul B. Mahol). video-trim.ts adapts libavfilter/trim.c.
packet-duration.ts adapts libavformat/mux.c guess_pkt_duration
(Copyright (c) 2000, 2001, 2002 Fabrice Bellard).
These adaptations retain LGPL-2.1-or-later and the accompanying license text.
They implement a bounded known-PTS video subset; codec-specific rate constraints,
unknown-PTS synchronization, keyframe flags and full diagnostic parity remain
unimplemented. Scheduling and replay integration do not complete the project-wide
license audit.

video-output/encoder-ratio.ts adapts av_reduce/av_d2q in libavutil/rational.c
(Copyright (c) 2003 Michael Niedermayer). clock-expression.ts adapts arithmetic
grammar in libavutil/eval.c (Copyright (c) 2002-2006 Michael Niedermayer;
Copyright (c) 2006 Oded Shimon). These adaptations retain LGPL-2.1-or-later.
General expression functions/state and exhaustive platform-libm
numeric equivalence remain incomplete.

video-output/encoder-sync-queue.ts adapts the video-frame synchronization queue
state machine in FFmpeg fftools/sync_queue.c at commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8, licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later. The public
TypeScript API adds bounded ownership and cleanup diagnostics for the runtime.
The developer-only oracle in tools/differential-runner/video-encoder-sync includes
that pinned source. Audio sample splitting/alignment and complete native
scheduler integration are not implemented by this video queue.

src/actor-video/ adds bounded actor input/output scheduling and explicit timed
rawvideo CLI execution. Detailed FFmpeg source functions and copyright provenance
are in src/actor-video/NOTICE.activation, under LGPL-2.1-or-later. The shared spool,
event serialization, asynchronous cancellation and failure aggregation are
EdgeFFmpeg additions. These ephemeral stores do not implement distributed restart
recovery. This does not complete the project-wide license/distribution audit.

actor-video/simple-command.ts additionally adapts finite rawvideo auto-selection
score/tie behavior from fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c map_auto_video at the same pinned
commit. Raw token boundary scanning follows libavutil/avstring.c av_get_token
(Copyright 2000, 2001, 2002 Fabrice Bellard; 2007 Mans Rullgard) and graphparser.c
(Copyright 2007 Bobby Bingham; 2008 Vitor Sessak), LGPL-2.1-or-later. It preserves
raw option text while rebinding existing topology edges without added filter nodes.
Packet-presence inference from finite rawvideo handle size, candidate preflight,
handle reuse and asynchronous cancellation are EdgeFFmpeg adaptations. This finite rawvideo behavior is covered by the scoped simple-video CLI
reference comparisons; it does not establish complete CLI conformance.

The simple filter selector adapter follows fftools/cmdutils.c
stream_specifier_parse/stream_specifier_match at the pinned commit, including
base-zero LP64 strtol saturation, signed32 narrowing and negative-index sentinel
matching for one declared rawvideo stream. General stream lists/metadata/program
selectors remain unimplemented. video-output/output-limit.ts now applies the actual
frame-time deadline from fftools/ffmpeg_enc.c check_recording_time instead of
predicting the next passthrough PTS; equal timestamps may still be within the limit.
LGPL-2.1-or-later; complete license text is in LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt.

video-output/option-order.ts and stream-option.ts adapt typed option ingestion,
last-matching per-stream string selection, and rawvideo format dictionary
overrides from fftools/cmdutils.c, ffmpeg_demux.c and ffmpeg_mux_init.c at
commit 946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.
video-output/input-rate-range.ts and its rawvideo execution callers adapt the
forced decoder cadence in fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c video_frame_process, keeping
the physical demux clock independent of the matching decoder rate and
streamcopy output clock. LGPL-2.1-or-later; the license text and pinned source
locations are listed above. This covers finite rawvideo with known timestamps;
general codec timebases and exact native diagnostic/exit-code parity remain
unimplemented. It does not complete the project-wide license audit.

raw-video.ts streamcopy output-option handling and output clock selection adapt
fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c new_stream_video and streamcopy_init at the same pinned
commit. Packet timestamps and durations are rescaled without frame duplication,
and encoder-only pixel/synchronization/timebase settings are ignored when copying.
The rate and maximum-rate options retain Native validation. LGPL-2.1-or-later.
This finite rawvideo path does not provide compressed-codec streamcopy or full
error/diagnostic parity, and does not complete the project-wide license audit.

The signed video time candidate adapts seek failure and buffered-packet flushing
from libavformat/seek.c seek_frame_generic and ff_read_frame_flush, and time
offset/trim setup from fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c at the pinned commit above.
Frame-count/probe-size arithmetic models the finite rawvideo default probe only.
Negative video start/stop values do not enable negative durations, audio timing,
custom probe settings or general protocol seek semantics. LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Seeking/index source attribution: libavformat/seek.c, Copyright (c) 2000, 2001,
2002 Fabrice Bellard; rawvideo demux source, Copyright (c) 2001 Fabrice Bellard.
Tentative EOF filter clocks additionally follow fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c fallback
parameter configuration at the pinned commit. Per-source decoded-state flags
and asynchronous fallback selection are EdgeFFmpeg runtime adaptations.

The copyts candidate adapts input timestamp offset/trim setup from
fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c and forced-rate processing from fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c
at commit946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Forced-rate initialization retains a physically seekable last packet even when
accurate input trim discards it; the bounded adapter decodes one packet solely
to initialize codec parameters and verify input identity. This does not implement
compressed-codec copyts, nonzero container start offsets or audio timestamp modes.

Automatic CFR/VSCFR selection follows fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c new_stream_video
at the same pinned commit. Global boolean suffix matching follows cmdutils.c
find_option/write_option. The private direct-output marker preserves that Native
frontend distinction through graph normalization. LGPL-2.1-or-later; the license
text and source location above apply. This does not complete distribution audit.


flac-selection.ts adapts the bounded one-input ordered/optional/negative map
semantics of opt_map in fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c and automatic/manual output stream
selection in fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c at FFmpeg commit
946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8. Original source and copyright notices
remain in upstream/ffmpeg; this adaptation retains LGPL-2.1-or-later with the
accompanying license text. It models one FLAC audio stream and attached-picture
identities. Bounded uppercase V, metadata, attached_pic disposition and explicit
usable-stream facts additionally follow stream_specifier_parse/match in
fftools/cmdutils.c (Copyright (c) 2000-2003 Fabrice Bellard), including metadata
token parsing before opt_map's optional remainder. General media selection
remains unimplemented. This notice does not complete the project-wide license audit.

flac-wave-time.ts and flac-transform.ts implement scoped timestamp/recording-time
policy with reference to fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c, ffmpeg_mux_init.c,
ffmpeg_filter.c and libavfilter/trim.c at the same pinned commit. The bounded
packet-copy route in flac-wave-remux.ts follows libavformat/flacenc.c and mux.c;
the original copyright/license notices remain in upstream/ffmpeg. Applicable
adaptations retain LGPL-2.1-or-later. Core ownership and atomic VFS publication
are EdgeFFmpeg-specific boundaries, not Native OS side-effect compatibility.

flac-copy-duration.ts additionally adapts the scoped stream-copy recording-time
checks in fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c (input_packet_process/ts_fixup) and
fftools/ffmpeg_mux.c (of_streamcopy) at the same pinned commit. The Native
microsecond DTS estimate uses av_rescale_q rounding. Original source notices
remain in upstream/ffmpeg; this adaptation retains LGPL-2.1-or-later.

flac-filter-rate.ts and the aformat/rate path in flac-transform.ts model scoped
automatic converter placement using fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c and
libavfilter/avfiltergraph.c at commit946fcce07b6dcd0331c8cc609192aeff5e1924f8.
Original copyright notices remain in upstream/ffmpeg; applicable adaptations
retain LGPL-2.1-or-later. The existing license text and source location apply.

flac-timed-buffered.ts composes finite filter execution with input/output trim
placement from fftools/ffmpeg_filter.c and libavfilter/trim.c at the same pinned
commit. Original source notices remain in upstream/ffmpeg; applicable adaptations
retain LGPL-2.1-or-later under the accompanying license text. Core allocation
ownership and atomic publication remain EdgeFFmpeg-specific boundaries.
